    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was done:\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n1. **Updated `generateReport()` function** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`):\n   - Added optional `thresholds` parameter that accepts an object like `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`\n   - For each threshold, compares the metric's score against the minimum\n   - Marks a threshold as failed if the metric has no score (null) or score < minimum\n   - Adds `passed` field to report (true if all thresholds pass)\n   - Adds `thresholds` array with entries: `{ metric, min, score, passed }`\n\n2. **Updated markdown report formatter** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`):\n   - Added \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL for each threshold with min/actual scores\n\n3. **Added test coverage** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`):\n   - Test: thresholds pass when all metrics meet minimums\n   - Test: report marked as failed when any threshold fails\n   - Test: metrics with null scores fail their thresholds\n   - Test: without thresholds, report has no `passed`/`thresholds` fields\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n1. **Updated eval command** (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`):\n   - Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option that can be used multiple times\n   - Parses thresholds into an array using Commander.js callback accumulator\n   - Validates threshold format: `<metric>=<number>`\n   - Validates threshold values: must be 0.0 to 1.0\n   - Validates metric IDs against available evaluations\n\n2. **Error handling** (`runEvalCommand` function):\n   - Exit code **1**: if any threshold fails (report still generated)\n   - Exit code **2**: if threshold is malformed or metric unknown (no report)\n   - Error messages list valid metric IDs for unknown metrics\n\n3. **Updated documentation**:\n   - Added `--threshold` option to both README files with usage examples\n\n### Testing\n\nManual testing verified:\n- \u2705 All thresholds pass \u2192 exit 0\n- \u2705 Any threshold fails \u2192 exit 1\n- \u2705 Malformed threshold \u2192 exit 2 with error message\n- \u2705 Unknown metric \u2192 exit 2 with valid metric IDs listed\n- \u2705 Invalid value (outside 0-1) \u2192 exit 2\n- \u2705 Metric with null score \u2192 fails threshold\n- \u2705 Multiple thresholds work correctly\n- \u2705 JSON and Markdown reports both include threshold info\n\nThe implementation is backward compatible: without `--threshold` options, reports and exit codes work exactly as before.",
